From a389621bd68c2b108e943b3eccf39131fc780787 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:18:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: support hyprland 0.57 workspace addresses

Hyprland 0.57 (hyprwm/Hyprland#16140, #16269) removed the global numeric
workspace id in favour of addressables. `hyprctl workspaces/activeworkspace/
monitors/clients -j` now send `address` and `type` (`normal`/`special`);
`id` only exists for numbered workspaces and unused special workspaces are
sent as {"address":"","type":"","name":""}. The socket2 `*v2` workspace
events start with the address (`3`, `foo`, `special:foo`) instead of the id.

This made deserialization fail with `missing field id` and made the event
listener die with `invalid integer` as soon as a named/special workspace
event arrived (which also stopped monitor/config reload handling).

hyprland-rs (vendored):
- `Workspace`/`WorkspaceBasic`: `id` is now `Option`, add `address` and
  `kind` (+ `is_special()`, `selector()`); output of older versions is
  converted (regular -> id as address, special -> name as address)
- workspace events and `WindowMoved` carry `address` and an optional `id`
  and no longer fail to parse for named/special workspaces
- add `WorkspaceKind` and `workspace_selector()`

hyprshell:
- `WorkspaceId` is now the workspace address (String) instead of `i32`,
  `Active` is no longer `Copy`
- sort workspaces via `workspace_sort_key()` (special, numbered, named)
  instead of relying on negative ids for special workspaces
- switch to workspaces from their address: numbered -> `N`,
  named -> `name:X`, special -> `special:X` (lua and legacy dispatchers)

Not tested against a live 0.57 session.
